# The settings screen's switches and printer row: snow, monochrome and
# BIOS output switched on, the printer port stepped to LPT2 with Space
# and the type PLAIN chosen from its F4 list; 10 page lines are refused
# with their range, the cursor staying on the field; then 72 page lines
# and labels 40 x 8 are saved, and the home screen after it is drawn in
# the monochrome palette.  The adapter and DOS version differ between
# machines and are masked.
#@ CFGHAS SNOW=1
#@ CFGHAS MONO=1
#@ CFGHAS BIOS=1
#@ CFGHAS PRINTER=LPT2
#@ CFGHAS PRTYPE=PLAIN
#@ CFGHAS PAGELEN=72
#@ CFGHAS LABELW=40
#@ CFGHAS LABELH=8
M 8 19 26
M 9 61 18
T ADMIN
K ENTER
T Retro1986
K ENTER
K ALT-O
T S
K TAB TAB TAB TAB SPACE TAB SPACE TAB SPACE TAB SPACE TAB F4
S TYPES
K DOWN ENTER TAB CTRL-Y
T 10
K ENTER
S RANGE
K CTRL-Y
T 72
K TAB CTRL-Y
T 40
K TAB CTRL-Y
T 8
K ENTER
S SAVED
K ESC
M CLEAR
S MONOHOME
K F3
T Y
